---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About this site and how it was rebuilt in Astro.">
  <div class="content">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      This site was originally a WordPress installation running the
      <strong>Hello Elementor</strong> theme — a lightweight, minimalist theme
      designed to pair with the Elementor page builder.
    </p>
    <p>
      It has been rebuilt with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a>, a modern
      framework for content-driven websites. The rebuild preserves the original
      theme's structure and design language while shipping as fast, static HTML.
    </p>

    <h2>What carried over</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The header with a primary navigation menu and an accessible mobile toggle.</li>
      <li>The footer with a secondary navigation menu and copyright.</li>
      <li>The 800px content width and 1200px wide layout from <code>theme.json</code>.</li>
      <li>Clean, system-font typography and a skip-to-content link.</li>
      <li>A blog with archive and single-post views.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How to edit content</h2>
    <p>
      Blog posts live as Markdown files in <code>src/content/blog/</code>. The site
      menus and identity are configured in <code>src/data/site.ts</code>, and the
      design tokens live in <code>src/styles/global.css</code>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
